<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Libyans</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Libyan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Libyans refers to the inhabitants of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a> and, in antiquity, to the indigenous Berber-speaking peoples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>, Libyan subjects were heavily taxed and supplied soldiers to Carthaginian armies, and their discontent fed revolts such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary-war">Mercenary War</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a>, Libyans faced colonial settlement and harsh repression.</p></div>
